    {
      "id": "claim_2ff07e76855944749086288a89fa1e46",
      "statement": "Fetch failures are indistinguishable from cache hits: fetchEndpoint() catches its own exceptions (including thrown non-OK HTTP statuses) and returns null, so an upstream 500 or network error is persisted as status NO_DELTA. status ERROR is written only for exceptions raised inside processEndpoint() itself, and that ERROR row stores contentHash: '' plus the message in errorMessage.",
