    {
      "id": "claim_5ab44c4a03ba47b5a38ea95b344dbfac",
      "statement": "The production composition runs the sync worker pull-only: the sync-worker service declares no build: and instead references the published image ghcr.io/fatpat81/beerhammer/forceorg-sync-worker:${FORCEORG_TAG:-latest}, kept under profiles: ['tools'] and gated on postgres: condition: service_healthy, so a prod host can run one-shot ETL passes with no source checkout while `docker compose up` still never starts it. The dev composition is the only one that builds Dockerfile.sync-worker locally.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile.sync-worker#L55-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc2a9d78c4819e0fb12818fdf44be5b1b823f9c675dc56acad302e4973d4513d:"
