    {
      "id": "claim_c7ddd199bcb9430d913e94ce0ce6b083",
      "statement": "The worker image is published to GHCR only. The GitHub deploy workflow builds Dockerfile.sync-worker on pushes to main and pushes forceorg-sync-worker:latest plus a commit-sha tag (the mechanism that makes FORCEORG_TAG pinning and sha rollback work), whereas the GitLab CI build-images stage builds and pushes only Dockerfile.web and Dockerfile.api, so a deployment sourcing images from GitLab has no sync-worker image and must use the source-build composition or the workflow instead.",
