    {
      "id": "claim_b5aebec8818546579c631d9a407a24ad",
      "statement": "In docker-compose.prod.yml the worker's DATABASE_URL and DIRECT_URL are interpolated from the same public Postgres placeholders the API service uses (${POSTGRES_USER:-postgres}, ${POSTGRES_DB:-forceorg_dev}), so the worker boots with zero configuration against placeholder credentials — unlike the API service in the same file, which sets no DIRECT_URL and depends on its entrypoint default. An asymmetry follows: the worker's DATABASE_URL falls back to ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:-postgrespassword} while its DIRECT_URL falls back to ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:-postgres}, so with no overrides the two URLs carry different passwords and the default DIRECT_URL is not a usable connection string; runs still work because the worker image only issues runtime queries over DATABASE_URL and performs no migrations.",
      "evidence": [
